{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-evidence-gate", "file": "references/post-rejection-guess-cycle.md", "content": "# Rejection does not localize the error

A continual-ARC instance had three demos, then a speculative output that moved displayed objects into the upper-left based on an assumed diagonal/translation arrangement. After it was rejected, subsequent submissions merely shifted the same shapes/lines among nearby placements or varied which continuation endpoint was used. All failed. Binary incorrect feedback does not reveal which cell or assumption is wrong, so this kind of parameter sweep is not evidence-driven.

After rejection, preserve and retire the complete prediction. Recompute exact deltas for every demo and audit the proposed transformation as a whole: selection, geometry/orientation, color and background behavior, and retention/removal of source objects. Submit only if a materially different coherent rule explains all demonstrations; do not treat another placement/color variant as a fresh hypothesis merely because it differs at a few cells. A demo cap does not justify guess cycling.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1790545205/attempts/52b150a3511a4455a56f31d31c01d91b/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-evidence-gate/references/post-rejection-guess-cycle.md"}

